Job Description – Senior Cost and Budget Accountant

Job Summary: We are seeking a highly analytical and detail-oriented Senior Cost and Budget Accountant to join our finance team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for overseeing cost analysis, budgeting processes, and financial planning activities. This role plays a critical part in guiding business decisions by preparing accurate cost reports, analyzing variances, and ensuring budgetary control across departments.

Key Responsibilities:

Develop and maintain the budget and cost accounting records, documents, and records of the organization in conformance with legal requirements &amp; accepted accounting principles and standards;
Analyze manufacturing costs and prepare regular reports comparing standard costs to actual production costs;
Monitoring unit cost variance and implementing cost standards for materials and labor;
Conduct cost-budget analysis and prepare regular reports comparing standard costs to actual production costs;
Manage and comply with tax filings and government reporting requirements;
Provide management with reports that specify and compare factors that affect the prices and profitability of products or services;
Review standard and actual costs for inaccuracies and perform life cycle cost-benefit analysis;
Collect cost information and maintain an expenses database to recommend costs and savings;
Prepare and complete internal cost audits and construct data accumulation systems;
Determine fixed costs (e.g., salaries, rent and insurance) and record variable costs (e.g., purchases of raw material and operations costs);
Reconciling beginning raw materials, work-in-progress and finished-goods stock;
Conduct physical inventories and monitor the cycle count program;
Prepare and analyze report profit margins and budgeting reports;
Prepares monthly, quarterly, and annual budget and cost statements;
Identify and recommend cost-effective solutions;
Requirements

Skills &amp; Abilities

Thorough knowledge of accounting procedures;
In-depth understanding of IFRS;
Experience with accounting software and MS Office;
Excellent analytical skills with an attention to detail;
Strong time management and organizational skills;
Integrity, with an ability to handle confidential information;
Academic Qualification

BA Degree in Accounting, Finance or a related field, preferably in the manufacturing sector
Years of experience: Minimum of 5+ years of experience

Location: Addis Ababa/ Dukem

Number required – 3 (Three) – Two for Dukem area and One for Addis Ababa area

Submission:  Interested applicants fulfilling the above requirements can submit their CV and copy of their credentials through our email address candidate@sariaconsult.com

Note: - Don't forget to write the position you are applying for in the subject line!

Job Address
Two for Dukem area and One for Addis Ababa area

